body:
Users cannot tell which model gives good results in the AI Chat panel. Our own local-model MCP benchmark (12 Ollama models, 20 tasks: read, change, multi-step + safety; run 2026-11-22, the issues from it are #3424 #3425 #3475 #3476 #3543 #3544 #3545 #3546) shows a wide spread. Out of 20: ornith-1.5:35b 16, nemotron-3.5-super 15, qwen3.8 15, qwen3-coder/qwen3.6/qwen3:4b 13, qwen3:8b 9, llama3.1:8b 3, phi4-mini 1. Small models mostly cannot change a project correctly. The reporter's first cloud session (Anthropic claude-sonnet-5-5, 2026-11-23) added a tool, a Face and a Contour op and set the cutting data correctly.

Wanted:
1. Expand the benchmark into a repeatable model evaluation:
   - the same task set, 3 runs per task;
   - the panel's default local models;
   - the cloud models of each provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini; cost per task recorded);
   - safety tasks weighted (refuse an absurd tool, Allow/Deny before a delete).
   Results go to a data file in the repo.
2. Ship that file as recommendations in the panel. Each model in the model list (#3783) gets a badge:
   - "Recommended": can change your project reliably;
   - "Questions only": reads well, changes unreliably;
   - "Not recommended";
   - plus one plain sentence on why (e.g. "fails most multi-step changes in our tests").
   A model that is not in the file shows "Not tested".
3. Each badge names the evaluation date and CamCraft version, so it can go stale visibly. The evaluation re-runs at each minor cut, or when the tool set changes.

Done means: the evaluation runs from one command and writes the data file. The panel shows the badge and sentence for tested models and "Not tested" for others. A test pins that every default model in the presets has an entry.

Builds on #3783 (model list). Reporter (2026-11-23): "we might want to expand that evaluation and put some sort of recommendations on the AI Chat property page ... like don't use model x because it will not give you good results".

User validation: before this merges, the reporter (mkinney) hand-tests a build of the PR in the desktop app. The PR stays a draft until that confirmation is on the PR.
